# CompanionSkills holds installable companion skills and their reference files
# (documentation), not Godot project code. This .gdignore keeps the editor from
# scanning the folder, so a reference such as
# mcp-extension-creator/references/example-extension.gd — a class_name'd
# MCPToolkitExtension shown as a copy-paste template — is never registered as a
# global class or auto-discovered as a live extension in this project (or in an
# end user's project once the addon is installed). Copy the template into your
# own extension location to activate it.
